. He has released one studio album and two EPs.","title":"Woo Won-jae","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woo_Won-jae"}},"Q486196":{"id":"Q486196","name":"Park Soo-ah","ko":"박수아","birthName":"Park Soo-young","birthNameEn":"Park Soo-young","aliases":["Park Soo-young","Lizzy"],"birth":"1992-07-31","death":"","birthplace":"Busan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":168,"occupations":["singer","film actor","dancer","television actor","model","actor"],"debut":"2010","agencies":[{"name":"Pledis Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q45282","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q181144","name":"Orange Caramel","start":"2010","end":"2016"},{"id":"Q389067","name":"After School","start":"2010","end":"2015"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/luvlyzzy/","x":"https://x.com/p_Lizzy","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/0c82e0fc-51c1-4415-8db8-3cb68b63e451"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Park Soo-young, is a South Korean singer and actress. She debuted under the stage name Lizzy (리지) as a member of the South Korean girl group After School in March 2010 and later formed part of the group's sub-units, Orange Caramel and After School Blue. She made her solo debut in January 2015 with the digital single \"Not an Easy Girl\". Outside of her music career, Park has starred in various television dramas, including All My Love (2011) and Angry Mom (2015). In May 2018, Park graduated from After School following the expiration of her contract, but remains a member of Orange Caramel. Following her departure, she shifted her work to acting and changed her stage name to Park Soo-ah (박수아).","title":"Park Soo-young (entertainer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park_Soo-young_%28entertainer%29"}},"Q52219380":{"id":"Q52219380","name":"Lucas","ko":"루카스 (가수)","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Wong Yuk-hei","Lucas Wong"],"birth":"1999-01-25","death":"","birthplace":"Sha Tin District","nationality":["People's Republic of China"],"height":null,"occupations":["rapper","singer"],"debut":"2018","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Universal Music Group","korean":false,"id":"Q38903","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q67972645","name":"NCT U","start":"2018","end":"2023"},{"id":"Q23725822","name":"NCT","start":"2018","end":"2023"},{"id":"Q66710876","name":"SuperM","start":"2019","end":"2021"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/lucas_xx444/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/958b3e1f-0ca5-43aa-a7f6-bc1143253fe9"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Wong Yuk-hei, known professionally as Lucas, is a Hong Kong rapper formerly signed under SM Entertainment. He is a former member of South Korean boy group NCT and its Chinese sub-unit WayV, and he was chosen by SM to be a member of the supergroup SuperM. He made his solo debut on 1 April 2024, with the single album Renegade.","title":"Lucas (rapper)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucas_%28rapper%29"}},"Q57599540":{"id":"Q57599540","name":"Maru","ko":"마루 (가수)","birthName":"이재준","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Jae-jun","Lee Jae Jun"],"birth":"1997-09-25","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q491944","name":"C-Clown","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jjun_iii__/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/7gOq63Sl8DqWQL83Fsn6sD"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q59594164":{"id":"Q59594164","name":"Kim Suhyeon","ko":"김수현","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Suhyeon","Kim Soo-hyun","Kim Su-hyeon","Kim Su-hyun","Kim Suhyun","Kim Su Hyun"],"birth":"2000-01-15","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["television actor","pop singer"],"debut":"2017-09-11","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q108888399","name":"Billlie","start":"2021","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/su_hyun1052/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/7de7827b-aa29-4bdf-890a-bd42c7490804"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q60991220":{"id":"Q60991220","name":"Rocky","ko":"라키","birthName":"Park Min-hyuk","birthNameEn":"Park Min-hyuk","aliases":["Park Min-hyuk","Rocky (South Korean Singer)"],"birth":"1999-02-25","death":"","birthplace":"Jinju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","dancer","rapper","songwriter","actor","model"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Fantagio","korean":true,"id":"Q13424955","start":"2016","end":"2023"}],"groups":[{"id":"Q23004252","name":"Astro","start":"2016","end":"2023"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/p_rocky/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/Park_Min-hyuk.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Park_Min-hyuk.png","author":"Crop/edit: User:SR5 Original: dispatchsns","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Park Min-hyuk, known professionally as Rocky (라키), is a South Korean rapper, singer-songwriter, actor and entrepreneur. He is a former member of the South Korean boy group Astro and its sub-unit Jinjin & Rocky. In 2023, he established and became the CEO of his own agency, Wonijin Entertainment, and debuted as a solo artist with the extended play (EP) Rockyst. Park made his acting debut in the web series To Be Continued (2015) and later gained recognition for his role in Broke Rookie Star (2022), for which he received multiple awards. He also starred in the Korean adaptation of the musical The Three Musketeers (2022).","title":"Rocky (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocky_%28singer%29"}},"Q7302004":{"id":"Q7302004","name":"Rebekah Kim","ko":"베카","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Bekah"],"birth":"1989-08-11","death":"","birthplace":"Honolulu","nationality":["United States","South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","songwriter","fashion designer"],"debut":"2009","agencies":[{"name":"Pledis Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q45282","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q389067","name":"After School","start":"2009","end":"2011"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/superbek/","x":"https://x.com/__bekah","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/a8c8300e-c768-4754-a05a-b90d50c19c72"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"After School was a South Korean girl group formed by Pledis Entertainment, with an admissions and graduation concept. After School officially debuted in January 2009 with the song \"Ah!\" from the single album New Schoolgirl. Following the addition of Uee in April of that year, they released \"Diva\", which won the \"Rookie of the Month\" award at the Cyworld Digital Music Awards. Pledis Entertainment then announced the graduation of Soyoung before adding Raina and Nana for the release \"Because of You\" in November 2009, which topped the monthly digital chart for December.","title":"Rebekah Kim","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebekah_Kim"}},"Q79404596":{"id":"Q79404596","name":"지수","ko":"","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"2003-11-22","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":[],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q48258503","name":"Busters","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q9021940":{"id":"Q9021940","name":"Baek Ye-rin","ko":"백예린","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Baek Yerin","Baek Ye Rin","Yerin Baek"],"birth":"1997-06-26","death":"","birthplace":"Daejeon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","lyricist","composer"],"debut":"2012","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q491777","name":"15&","start":"2012","end":"2019"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/yerin_the_genuine/","x":"https://x.com/yerinbaek","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/6dhfy4ByARPJdPtMyrUYJK","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/d598652a-b64a-4e21-b607-bcec71698731"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Baek Ye-rin, anglicized as Yerin Baek, is a South Korean singer-songwriter. A former member of South Korean duo 15&, she debuted as a solo artist with her extended play, Frank, in 2015. Baek is credited with writing and composition for the majority of her songs, often touching on personal topics and real-life experiences. In addition to her solo career, she is also the lead vocalist and guitarist for the South Korean rock band The Volunteers and has been performing with them since 2018.","title":"Yerin Baek","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yerin_Baek"}},"Q97303476":{"id":"Q97303476","name":"Kim Hee-jung","ko":"김희정","birthName":"김희정","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Aini","Kim Hee Jeong"],"birth":"1991-06-13","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["model"],"debut":"2006","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q60994549","name":"Pink Fantasy","start":"2018","end":"2020"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/aini_official_md/"},"photo":null,"bio":null}}}